//@version=6
indicator("Balu Zone Scalper v2.2", shorttitle="Balu v2.2", overlay=true, max_boxes_count=200, max_labels_count=400, max_lines_count=100)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// v2 CHANGES (see Script_Review_Balu_Hybrid.md)
//   - Golden Line "VWAP" falls back to a session TWAP (or proxy-symbol volume) when the
//     chart has no volume. On NSE:NIFTY spot v1's ta.vwap was na, so Regime was always
//     NEUTRAL and the regime alerts never fired.
//   - HTF swings are read from COMPLETED HTF bars only ([1] + lookahead_on) and added
//     once per HTF bar, so zones no longer appear live and then vanish on reload.
//   - Flow slope is built from per-bar delta, so the daily reset of the cumulative
//     line no longer shows up as a fake FALLING/RISING spike near the open.
//   - Path history starts only on confirmed state changes, with one active episode
//     across ALL states. Timeouts, ambiguous bars and session cuts remain visible.
//     Counts are descriptive, not independent samples or a forecast of trade success.
//   - Regime / divergence / pressure alerts fire on the bar close; separate EARLY
//     pressure alerts are available for the forming bar (these can cancel).
//   v2.1 FIXES
//   - A zone beyond its tier's reach cap gives way to nearer fresh structure, so "To Supply/Demand" tracks price.
//   - Spent (mitigated) zones are hidden by default; if kept, they stop where they broke and lose their label.
//   - Golden Line and Moving Line no longer bridge from the prior session or across warm-up.
//   v2.2 CLEANUP
//   - Sweep × markers are CONFIRMED by default: the × prints on the bar that closes beyond the
//     sweep bar's high (demand) / low (supply) within N bars, once per level area per session.
//     Confirmation reduces repeated probes; it is not evidence of profitable entries.
//     Untick "Confirmed Sweeps Only" for raw markers.
//   - New same-side zones respect "Min Zone Spacing x ATR" at creation. Existing zones
//     stay fixed as ATR changes; projections that cannot fit inside the reach cap are skipped.
//   - Opening-range high / low drawn as key-level rails (ORH / ORL) once the range completes.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// BALU ZONE SCALPER — adaptive zone map + descriptive path history
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Rebuilt so the read is available WHILE the move happens, not after it.
//
//   1) ZONE MAP
//        → Supply/demand bands are drawn from a LIVE POOL of confirmed levels:
//          chart-timeframe swings (fast — they confirm in a few bars), plus
//          higher-timeframe swings, prior-day H/L/C and the opening range as
//          slower context. Nearby levels MERGE into one averaged level instead
//          of stacking into three near-identical zones (no strength is tracked).
//        → The map is maintained every confirmed bar, so a trend day always has
//          a next zone beyond price instead of running off the end of a map that
//          was frozen at the open.
//        → Reach caps apply to EVERY tier. When no real structure sits inside the
//          cap, the zone is drawn as PROJECTED (dotted, labelled "proj") so a
//          measured offset is never mistaken for an actual level.
//
//   2) MOVING LINE
//        → Session-anchored estimated cumulative delta. The plotted line is scaled
//          into the session price range, which changes over time. Divergence uses
//          the raw series, not the changing visual scale. The opening bars are
//          suppressed while the scale has too little range.
//        → On an index feed with no usable volume this is a range-weighted PROXY
//          for pressure, not true bid/ask delta. It is labelled as such.
//
//   3) GOLDEN LINE
//        → Price anchor with a hysteresis band. Direction persists inside the band;
//          the regime is neutral when direction and the line's slope disagree.
//
//   PATH HISTORY
//        Only transitions with real zones on both sides start an episode. Barriers
//        are frozen at entry; the next 1..H bars are observed, never the entry bar.
//        Only one episode is active globally; transitions while busy are skipped.
//        The resolved-only share excludes timeouts, so the panel also shows bounds
//        over ALL finished episodes. These are accounting bounds, NOT confidence
//        intervals. Serial dependence and state selection prevent an iid Wilson
//        interval or an effective-sample-size claim. No validated edge is displayed.
//        The infinite-horizon distance formula is NOT a finite-horizon baseline.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §1 INPUTS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ── Zone Map ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpZone = "1) Zone Map"
showZones    = input.bool(true,  "Show Zones", group=grpZone)
sessionStr   = input.session("0915-1530", "Trading Session", group=grpZone, tooltip="Defines the session used for the day open, the opening range and every session-anchored series.")
swingLen     = input.int(3, "Swing Strength (chart TF)", minval=1, maxval=10, group=grpZone, tooltip="Bars each side to confirm a CHART-timeframe swing. This is the fast structure source: it confirms in this many bars, so the map tracks today's move instead of yesterday's.")
zoneTiers    = input.int(2, "Zones Per Side", minval=1, maxval=4, group=grpZone, tooltip="How many live supply and demand zones to keep beyond price at all times.")
zoneThickATR = input.float(0.35, "Zone Thickness x ATR", minval=0.05, maxval=2.0, step=0.05, group=grpZone, tooltip="Half-height of a zone in CHART-timeframe ATR, so a zone stays narrower than the move you are trading.")
capBaseATR   = input.float(2.5, "Tier 1 Reach Cap x ATR", minval=0.5, maxval=20.0, step=0.5, group=grpZone, tooltip="The first zone may never sit further than this from price.")
capStepATR   = input.float(2.5, "Extra Reach Per Tier x ATR", minval=0.5, maxval=20.0, step=0.5, group=grpZone, tooltip="Each further tier may add this much reach. Caps apply to EVERY tier, not only the first.")
orMinutes    = input.int(15, "Opening Range Minutes", minval=1, maxval=120, group=grpZone, tooltip="The opening-range high and low are added to the level pool as candidate zones.")
dedupeATR    = input.float(0.50, "Merge Levels Within x ATR", minval=0.05, maxval=3.0, step=0.05, group=grpZone, tooltip="Levels closer than this are merged into ONE level at their average price, instead of stacking into several near-identical zones. Merging does not make a level stronger.")
minSpaceATR  = input.float(1.0, "Min Zone Spacing x ATR", minval=0.0, maxval=5.0, step=0.1, group=grpZone, tooltip="Minimum center-to-center spacing when a new zone is added, against all live zones on that side. Existing levels stay fixed as ATR changes. A projected tier is omitted if spacing would exceed its reach cap. 0 disables the extra ATR spacing, not the zone-thickness gap.")
pruneATR     = input.float(14.0, "Forget Levels Beyond x ATR", minval=3.0, maxval=60.0, step=1.0, group=grpZone)
keepMitigated = input.bool(false, "Keep Mitigated Zones Visible", group=grpZone, tooltip="On = a spent zone stays on the chart, dimmed and ending where it broke. Off (v2.1 default) = it is removed, to reduce clutter.")
showZoneLbl  = input.bool(true,  "Show Zone Labels", group=grpZone)

// ── Higher-Timeframe Context ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpHtf = "2) Higher-Timeframe Context"
useHtfLevels = input.bool(true, "Add HTF Swings To Level Pool", group=grpHtf, tooltip="HTF swings are strong but confirm slowly, so here they are ONE input to the pool rather than the only source of the map.")
htfMode      = input.string("Auto", "HTF Source", options=["Auto", "15m", "30m", "1H", "2H", "4H", "Daily"], group=grpHtf)
htfPivotLen  = input.int(2, "HTF Swing Strength", minval=1, maxval=10, group=grpHtf, tooltip="Lower = faster confirmation. A 30m HTF at strength 2 confirms in about an hour; at strength 3 it takes 90 minutes or more.")

// ── Golden Line ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpGold = "3) Golden Line"
showGold     = input.bool(true,  "Show Golden Line", group=grpGold)
goldSource   = input.string("VWAP (session)", "Golden Line Source", options=["VWAP (session)", "Daily Pivot (PP)", "EMA"], group=grpGold, tooltip="Default is session VWAP, a moving fair-value line. Daily Pivot is a single static level for the day; EMA is a smooth trend anchor.")
goldEmaLen   = input.int(50, "EMA Length (if EMA)", minval=5, maxval=400, group=grpGold)
goldDeadATR  = input.float(0.25, "Regime Deadband x ATR", minval=0.0, maxval=2.0, step=0.05, group=grpGold, tooltip="Price must clear the line by this much to flip direction. Inside the band the last direction is retained (hysteresis); regime also checks the line's slope.")
goldTint     = input.bool(false, "Tint Background by Regime", group=grpGold)
goldProxy    = input.bool(false, "No Chart Volume: Use Proxy Symbol Volume", group=grpGold, tooltip="Off = equal-bar session TWAP when the chart has no volume, e.g. NSE:NIFTY spot. On = weight spot prices by another symbol's volume, not that symbol's VWAP. Neither mode establishes predictive edge.")
goldProxySym = input.symbol("NSE:NIFTY1!", "Proxy Volume Symbol", group=grpGold)

// ── Moving Line (Cumulative Delta) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
grpCVD = "4) Moving Line"
showCVD      = input.bool(true,  "Show Moving Line", group=grpCVD)
cvdSource    = input.string("Auto", "Delta Source", options=["Auto", "Real Volume", "Price Action"], group=grpCVD, tooltip="Auto uses real volume when the feed supplies it, else a range-weighted proxy. On an index feed this is a PROXY for pressure, not true bid/ask delta.")
flowWarmBars = input.int(10, "Minimum Bars Before Plotting", minval=2, maxval=120, group=grpCVD, tooltip="Suppresses the opening bars, where a session-anchored rescale has too little range to carry information.")
flowSmoothLen = input.int(5, "Flow Smoothing", minval=1, maxval=50, group=grpCVD)
flowSlopeLen = input.int(5, "Flow Slope Lookback", minval=1, maxval=50, group=grpCVD, tooltip="Flow direction is the smoothed delta summed over this many bars, not a single-bar tick. v2 builds it from per-bar delta so the daily reset of the line cannot create a fake move.")
flowDead     = input.float(0.30, "Flow Neutral Deadband", minval=0.0, maxval=2.0, step=0.05, group=grpCVD, tooltip="The slope must exceed this many standard deviations to read RISING or FALLING. Inside the band flow reads FLAT.")
showDiv      = input.bool(true,  "Detect Divergence", group=grpCVD)
divPivotLen  = input.int(5, "Divergence Pivot Lookback", minval=2, maxval=20, group=grpCVD, tooltip="A divergence can only be known this many bars AFTER the swing, so it is drawn on the bar where it became known.")

// ── Intrabar Pressure ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpFoot = "5) Intrabar Pressure"
showFootprint = input.bool(true, "Show Intrabar Pressure", group=grpFoot, tooltip="Marks candles whose lower-timeframe flow was strongly one-sided. This is intrabar pressure — it is not evidence of institutional activity.")
fpLtf         = input.timeframe("1", "Intrabar Resolution", group=grpFoot, tooltip="Must be STRICTLY lower than the chart timeframe. On a 1-minute chart there is nothing to look inside, and the reading is suppressed.")
fpMinSubBars  = input.int(3, "Minimum Sub-Bars", minval=2, maxval=60, group=grpFoot, tooltip="If fewer sub-bars are returned the reading is suppressed rather than reported from a one-bar sample.")
fpImbal       = input.float(0.50, "Imbalance Threshold", minval=0.1, maxval=0.95, step=0.01, group=grpFoot, tooltip="Net signed effort as a fraction of total effort. Each sub-bar is weighted by its CLOSE POSITION, not merely its colour.")
fpEffMult     = input.float(1.3, "Min Effort x Average", minval=0.5, maxval=5.0, step=0.1, group=grpFoot)
fpEffLen      = input.int(20, "Effort Average Lookback", minval=5, maxval=100, group=grpFoot)
fpAtZoneOnly  = input.bool(true, "Only Mark at Zones", group=grpFoot)
fpMarkTraps   = input.bool(true, "Mark Zone Sweeps", group=grpFoot)
sweepConfOnly = input.bool(true, "Confirmed Sweeps Only", group=grpFoot, tooltip="v2.2: a sweep (wick through a zone edge, close back inside) only prints its × when a later bar closes beyond the sweep bar's high (demand) / low (supply) within the bars below, and only once per zone per session. The × sits on the CONFIRMING bar. Off = v2.1 raw markers on the sweep bar.")
sweepConfBars = input.int(3, "Sweep Confirm Within Bars", minval=1, maxval=20, group=grpFoot)

// ── Path History ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpProb = "6) Path History (not a forecast)"
useProb      = input.bool(true, "Measure Path History", group=grpProb, tooltip="One episode on a confirmed state change with real zones on both sides, only when no other episode is active. Resolution does not restart an unchanged state. Counts are not independent evidence.")
probHorizon  = input.int(20, "Resolution Horizon (bars)", minval=3, maxval=200, group=grpProb, tooltip="Inspect the next 1..H bars, including bar H. No hit by H is a timeout. Both sides on one bar are ambiguous. A session boundary censors any unfinished episode.")
probMinN     = input.int(100, "Minimum Finished Episodes To Show %", minval=5, maxval=1000, group=grpProb, tooltip="A display threshold only, NOT an effective sample size or a guarantee of statistical significance. Counts remain visible below it; no calibrated forecast or confidence interval is claimed.")

// ── Key Levels ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpKey = "7) Key Levels"
showKeyLevels = input.bool(true,  "Show Key Levels", group=grpKey)
klPDHL        = input.bool(true,  "Prior-Day High / Low", group=grpKey)
klPDC         = input.bool(true,  "Prior-Day Close", group=grpKey)
klPivot       = input.bool(false, "Daily Pivot (PP / R1 / S1)", group=grpKey)
klOR          = input.bool(true,  "Opening Range High / Low", group=grpKey, tooltip="Drawn as ORH / ORL once the 'Opening Range Minutes' window has closed.")
klORClr       = input.color(color.new(#ff9800, 0), "Opening Range Color", group=grpKey)
klHLClr       = input.color(color.new(#00bcd4, 0), "PDH / PDL / PDC Color", group=grpKey)
klPivClr      = input.color(color.new(#7e57c2, 0), "Pivot Color", group=grpKey)

// ── Panel ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpRead = "8) Panel"
showPanel    = input.bool(true,  "Show Panel", group=grpRead)
panelPos     = input.string("Top Right", "Panel Position", options=["Top Left", "Top Center", "Top Right", "Bottom Left", "Bottom Center", "Bottom Right"], group=grpRead)
zoneProxATR  = input.float(0.35, "Zone Proximity x ATR", minval=0.05, maxval=2.0, step=0.05, group=grpRead, tooltip="How close price must be to a zone to count as 'at' it.")

// ── Colors ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpClr = "9) Colors"
supplyClr = input.color(color.new(#ef5350, 0), "Supply", group=grpClr)
demandClr = input.color(color.new(#26a69a, 0), "Demand", group=grpClr)
goldClr   = input.color(color.new(#ffa726, 0), "Golden Line", group=grpClr)
cvdUpClr  = input.color(color.new(#26c281, 0), "Moving Line Up", group=grpClr)
cvdDnClr  = input.color(color.new(#e74c3c, 0), "Moving Line Down", group=grpClr)
neutralClr = input.color(color.new(#9e9e9e, 0), "Neutral", group=grpClr)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §2 CORE SERIES
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
atr      = ta.atr(14)
rangeBar = math.max(high - low, syminfo.mintick)
tfMin    = math.max(timeframe.in_seconds() / 60.0, 1.0)
isIntraday = timeframe.isintraday

// The session input now actually drives the day, so pre/post-market bars cannot
// seed the opening range or reset the delta.
inSession    = isIntraday ? not na(time(timeframe.period, sessionStr)) : true
newTradingDay = timeframe.change("D")
isNewSession = isIntraday ? (inSession and (not inSession[1] or newTradingDay)) : newTradingDay
sessionEnds = isIntraday and inSession and (session.islastbar or na(time(timeframe.period, sessionStr, bars_back=-1)))

// Prior-day H/L/C — non-repainting idiom (completed previous day via [1] + lookahead).
[pdH, pdL, pdC] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", [high[1], low[1], close[1]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)

// Prior-day floor-trader pivots (the "daily levels" — different every day).
pp = (pdH + pdL + pdC) / 3.0
r1 = 2 * pp - pdL
s1 = 2 * pp - pdH

// ── Session anchors ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var float orHigh  = na
var float orLow   = na
var float sessHi  = na
var float sessLo  = na
var int   dayLen  = 0
orBars = math.max(1, math.ceil(orMinutes / tfMin))

if isNewSession
    orHigh  := high
    orLow   := low
    sessHi  := high
    sessLo  := low
    dayLen  := 1
else if inSession
    dayLen += 1
    sessHi := math.max(nz(sessHi, high), high)
    sessLo := math.min(nz(sessLo, low), low)
    if dayLen <= orBars
        orHigh := math.max(nz(orHigh, high), high)
        orLow  := math.min(nz(orLow, low), low)

// ── Structure sources ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Chart-timeframe swings confirm in swingLen bars — minutes, not hours. This is
// what keeps the map current; HTF swings are slower context, not the only source.
sPH = ta.pivothigh(high, swingLen, swingLen)
sPL = ta.pivotlow(low, swingLen, swingLen)

autoHtfRes = tfMin <= 3 ? "15" : tfMin <= 5 ? "30" : tfMin <= 15 ? "60" : tfMin <= 60 ? "240" : "D"
htfRes = htfMode == "15m" ? "15" : htfMode == "30m" ? "30" : htfMode == "1H" ? "60" : htfMode == "2H" ? "120" : htfMode == "4H" ? "240" : htfMode == "Daily" ? "D" : autoHtfRes
if barstate.isfirst and useHtfLevels and timeframe.in_seconds(htfRes) <= timeframe.in_seconds()
    runtime.error("HTF Source must be strictly higher than the chart timeframe.")
// v2: read the swing from the previous COMPLETED HTF bar ([1] + lookahead_on). The value is
// then fixed for the whole HTF bar and identical live and on reload (v1 could repaint).
htfPH = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfRes, ta.pivothigh(htfPivotLen, htfPivotLen)[1], gaps=barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
htfPL = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfRes, ta.pivotlow(htfPivotLen, htfPivotLen)[1],  gaps=barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
htfNewBar = timeframe.change(htfRes)

// ── Level pool ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// One pool of candidate levels. Levels within the merge tolerance combine into a
// single level instead of stacking into several near-identical zones.
var array<float> lvlPrice  = array.new<float>()
var array<bool>  lvlIsHigh = array.new<bool>()

f_addLevel(_p, _isHigh) =>
    if not na(_p) and _p > 0 and not na(atr) and atr > 0
        float tol = atr * dedupeATR
        int hit = -1
        if lvlPrice.size() > 0
            for i = 0 to lvlPrice.size() - 1
                if lvlIsHigh.get(i) == _isHigh and math.abs(lvlPrice.get(i) - _p) <= tol
                    hit := i
                    break
        if hit >= 0
            lvlPrice.set(hit, (lvlPrice.get(hit) + _p) / 2.0)
        else
            lvlPrice.push(_p)
            lvlIsHigh.push(_isHigh)

f_prunePool() =>
    if lvlPrice.size() > 0 and not na(atr) and atr > 0
        float far = atr * pruneATR
        for i = lvlPrice.size() - 1 to 0
            if math.abs(lvlPrice.get(i) - close) > far
                lvlPrice.remove(i)
                lvlIsHigh.remove(i)
    while lvlPrice.size() > 60
        lvlPrice.shift()
        lvlIsHigh.shift()

if barstate.isconfirmed
    f_addLevel(sPH, true)
    f_addLevel(sPL, false)
    if useHtfLevels and htfNewBar
        f_addLevel(htfPH, true)
        f_addLevel(htfPL, false)
    if isNewSession
        f_addLevel(pdH, true)
        f_addLevel(pdL, false)
        f_addLevel(pdC, true)
        f_addLevel(pdC, false)
    if dayLen == orBars + 1
        f_addLevel(orHigh, true)
        f_addLevel(orLow, false)
    f_prunePool()

// Nearest pooled level above / below a reference (at least _gap from it), skipping any
// level within _space of a zone already on that side.
f_nearestAbove(_ref, _gap, _used, _space) =>
    float best = na
    if lvlPrice.size() > 0
        for i = 0 to lvlPrice.size() - 1
            float v = lvlPrice.get(i)
            if v > _ref + _gap and (na(best) or v < best)
                bool taken = false
                if _used.size() > 0
                    for j = 0 to _used.size() - 1
                        if math.abs(_used.get(j) - v) <= _space
                            taken := true
                            break
                if not taken
                    best := v
    best

f_nearestBelow(_ref, _gap, _used, _space) =>
    float best = na
    if lvlPrice.size() > 0
        for i = 0 to lvlPrice.size() - 1
            float v = lvlPrice.get(i)
            if v < _ref - _gap and (na(best) or v > best)
                bool taken = false
                if _used.size() > 0
                    for j = 0 to _used.size() - 1
                        if math.abs(_used.get(j) - v) <= _space
                            taken := true
                            break
                if not taken
                    best := v
    best

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §3 GOLDEN LINE  (regime with hysteresis)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// v2: session-anchored weighted average with a no-volume fallback. On an index feed
// (volume 0) ta.vwap is na, which froze Regime at NEUTRAL in v1. Weights: chart volume
// if the feed has it, else proxy-symbol volume (optional), else 1 per bar (= TWAP).
var bool volSeen = false
volSeen := volSeen or (not na(volume) and volume > 0)
goldProxyVol = request.security(goldProxySym, timeframe.period, volume, gaps=barmerge.gaps_on, lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off, ignore_invalid_symbol=true)
var float gChartPV = 0.0
var float gChartW = 0.0
var float gProxyPV = 0.0
var float gProxyW = 0.0
var float gSumP  = 0.0
var int   gCnt   = 0
if isNewSession
    gChartPV := 0.0
    gChartW := 0.0
    gProxyPV := 0.0
    gProxyW := 0.0
    gSumP  := 0.0
    gCnt   := 0
if inSession
    gChartPV += hlc3 * nz(volume)
    gChartW += nz(volume)
    gProxyPV += hlc3 * nz(goldProxyVol)
    gProxyW += nz(goldProxyVol)
    gSumP += hlc3
    gCnt += 1
vwapVal = gChartW > 0 ? gChartPV / gChartW : goldProxy and gProxyW > 0 ? gProxyPV / gProxyW : gCnt > 0 ? gSumP / gCnt : na
goldAnchorTxt = goldSource == "Daily Pivot (PP)" ? "Daily PP" : goldSource == "EMA" ? "EMA" : gChartW > 0 ? "VWAP" : goldProxy and gProxyW > 0 ? "Proxy weighted" : goldProxy ? "Proxy unavailable: TWAP" : "TWAP (no vol)"
goldVal = goldSource == "VWAP (session)" ? vwapVal : goldSource == "Daily Pivot (PP)" ? pp : ta.ema(close, goldEmaLen)

// Direction is retained inside the deadband; reset it with the session anchor.
goldDead = atr * goldDeadATR
var int goldState = 0
if isNewSession
    goldState := 0
if close > goldVal + goldDead
    goldState := 1
else if close < goldVal - goldDead
    goldState := -1

goldSlope = dayLen > flowSlopeLen ? goldVal - goldVal[flowSlopeLen] : 0.0
regimeIdx = goldState > 0 ? (goldSlope >= 0 ? 2 : 1) : goldState < 0 ? (goldSlope <= 0 ? 0 : 1) : 1
regimeTxt = regimeIdx == 2 ? "BULL" : regimeIdx == 0 ? "BEAR" : "NEUTRAL"
regimeClr = regimeIdx == 2 ? demandClr : regimeIdx == 0 ? supplyClr : neutralClr

// v2.1: break the line at each session open instead of drawing a diagonal from yesterday's value.
plot(showGold and not (isIntraday and isNewSession) ? goldVal : na, "Golden Line", color=goldClr, linewidth=2, style=plot.style_linebr)
bgcolor(goldTint and isIntraday ? color.new(regimeClr, 94) : na, title="Regime Tint")

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §4 MOVING LINE  (session cumulative delta)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
useRealVol = cvdSource == "Real Volume" or (cvdSource == "Auto" and volSeen)
closePos   = (close - low) / rangeBar
deltaSize  = useRealVol ? nz(volume) : rangeBar
barDelta   = deltaSize * (2 * closePos - 1)

var float cvd = 0.0
if inSession
    cvd := isNewSession ? barDelta : cvd + barDelta

// Session-anchored extremes: the rescale window only grows within the day, so the
// line cannot whipsaw across the pane the way a short rolling window does.
var float cvdHi = na
var float cvdLo = na
cvdHi := isNewSession ? cvd : math.max(nz(cvdHi, cvd), cvd)
cvdLo := isNewSession ? cvd : math.min(nz(cvdLo, cvd), cvd)

cvdSpan   = math.max(cvdHi - cvdLo, 1e-9)
priceSpan = math.max(nz(sessHi, high) - nz(sessLo, low), syminfo.mintick)
flowReady = dayLen >= flowWarmBars and (cvdHi - cvdLo) > 0

// A per-bar rescale, not a fixed transformation across time. Divergence uses raw cvd.
movingLine = nz(sessLo, low) + (cvd - cvdLo) / cvdSpan * priceSpan

// Smooth per-bar changes instead of a reset cumulative series. Normalized pressure,
// not a mean-centred z-score or a statistical significance test.
cvdSlope  = math.sum(ta.ema(barDelta, flowSmoothLen), flowSlopeLen)
slopeSd   = ta.stdev(cvdSlope, 100)
flowZ     = slopeSd > 0 ? cvdSlope / slopeSd : 0.0
flowState = flowZ > flowDead ? 1 : flowZ < -flowDead ? -1 : 0
flowTxt   = flowState > 0 ? "RISING" : flowState < 0 ? "FALLING" : "FLAT"
flowClr   = flowState > 0 ? cvdUpClr : flowState < 0 ? cvdDnClr : neutralClr

plot(showCVD and flowReady ? movingLine : na, "Moving Line", color=flowClr, linewidth=2, style=plot.style_steplinebr)

// ── Divergence ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ph = ta.pivothigh(high, divPivotLen, divPivotLen)
pl = ta.pivotlow(low, divPivotLen, divPivotLen)

var float lastPH    = na
var float lastPHcvd = na
var float lastPL    = na
var float lastPLcvd = na

if isNewSession
    lastPH    := na
    lastPHcvd := na
    lastPL    := na
    lastPLcvd := na

bearDiv = false
bullDiv = false
if showDiv and barstate.isconfirmed and dayLen > divPivotLen * 2 and not na(ph)
    float curCvd = cvd[divPivotLen]
    if not na(lastPH) and ph > lastPH and curCvd < lastPHcvd
        bearDiv := true
    lastPH    := ph
    lastPHcvd := curCvd
if showDiv and barstate.isconfirmed and dayLen > divPivotLen * 2 and not na(pl)
    float curCvd = cvd[divPivotLen]
    if not na(lastPL) and pl < lastPL and curCvd > lastPLcvd
        bullDiv := true
    lastPL    := pl
    lastPLcvd := curCvd

// Drawn on the bar where the divergence became knowable, not back on the swing,
// so the chart never implies the read was available earlier than it was.
plotshape(bearDiv, "Bearish Divergence", style=shape.triangledown, location=location.abovebar, color=supplyClr, size=size.tiny)
plotshape(bullDiv, "Bullish Divergence", style=shape.triangleup,   location=location.belowbar, color=demandClr, size=size.tiny)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §5 ZONE MAP  (maintained continuously — always a next zone beyond price)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
type Zone
    box   bx
    label lb
    float top
    float bot
    float center
    bool  isDemand
    bool  isProjected
    bool  mitigated

var array<Zone> zones = array.new<Zone>()

f_dropZone(_i) =>
    Zone z = zones.get(_i)
    if not na(z.bx)
        box.delete(z.bx)
    if not na(z.lb)
        label.delete(z.lb)
    zones.remove(_i)

f_makeZone(_center, _isDemand, _projected) =>
    float half = math.max(atr * zoneThickATR, syminfo.mintick * 4)
    float zt = _center + half
    float zb = _center - half
    color baseClr = _isDemand ? demandClr : supplyClr
    box bx = na
    label lb = na
    if showZones
        bx := box.new(bar_index, zt, bar_index, zb, border_color=color.new(baseClr, _projected ? 55 : 25), bgcolor=color.new(baseClr, _projected ? 90 : 80), border_width=1, border_style=_projected ? line.style_dotted : line.style_solid, xloc=xloc.bar_index, extend=extend.right)
        if showZoneLbl
            lb := label.new(bar_index, _center, (_isDemand ? "Demand" : "Supply") + (_projected ? " (proj)" : ""), xloc=xloc.bar_index, style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(baseClr, _projected ? 60 : 30), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
    zones.push(Zone.new(bx, lb, zt, zb, _center, _isDemand, _projected, false))

// Housekeeping: mark spent zones, retire far ones, and let a projected zone give
// way as soon as real structure is confirmed.
structureChanged = not na(sPH) or not na(sPL)
if barstate.isconfirmed and zones.size() > 0 and not na(atr) and atr > 0
    float far = atr * pruneATR
    for i = zones.size() - 1 to 0
        Zone z = zones.get(i)
        if not z.mitigated
            bool through = z.isDemand ? close < z.bot : close > z.top
            if through
                z.mitigated := true
                if not na(z.bx)
                    box.set_bgcolor(z.bx, color.new(color.gray, 88))
                    box.set_border_color(z.bx, color.new(color.gray, 55))
                    box.set_border_style(z.bx, line.style_dotted)
                    // v2.1: a spent zone ends where it broke instead of extending across the chart.
                    box.set_extend(z.bx, extend.none)
                    box.set_right(z.bx, bar_index)
                if not na(z.lb)
                    label.delete(z.lb)
                    z.lb := na
        bool stale = z.isProjected and not z.mitigated and structureChanged
        if stale or (z.mitigated and not keepMitigated) or math.abs(z.center - close) > far
            f_dropZone(i)

// Rebuild whichever side is short, so a trend day never runs off the end of its map.
if barstate.isconfirmed and not na(atr) and atr > 0 and (not isIntraday or inSession)
    float gap = math.max(atr * zoneThickATR * 2.0, atr * 0.25)
    // v2.2: same-side spacing, checked against EVERY live zone on that side (including one price is inside).
    float space = math.max(gap, atr * minSpaceATR)
    array<float> usedUp = array.new<float>()
    array<float> usedDn = array.new<float>()
    array<float> spaceUp = array.new<float>()
    array<float> spaceDn = array.new<float>()
    int haveUp = 0
    int haveDn = 0
    if zones.size() > 0
        for i = 0 to zones.size() - 1
            Zone z = zones.get(i)
            if not z.mitigated
                if z.isDemand
                    spaceDn.push(z.center)
                else
                    spaceUp.push(z.center)
                if not z.isDemand and z.bot > close
                    haveUp += 1
                    usedUp.push(z.center)
                if z.isDemand and z.top < close
                    haveDn += 1
                    usedDn.push(z.center)
    // v2.1: when the farthest live zone sits beyond its tier's reach cap, a fresh real level nearer
    // to price replaces it. Before, old far zones could fill every tier while new structure near
    // price was ignored ("To Demand 163").
    if haveUp >= zoneTiers
        float candUp = f_nearestAbove(close, gap, spaceUp, space)
        float farUp = usedUp.max()
        if not na(candUp) and candUp < farUp and farUp - close > atr * (capBaseATR + capStepATR * (haveUp - 1))
            for i = zones.size() - 1 to 0
                Zone z = zones.get(i)
                if not z.mitigated and not z.isDemand and z.center == farUp
                    f_dropZone(i)
                    break
            usedUp.remove(usedUp.indexof(farUp))
            spaceUp.remove(spaceUp.indexof(farUp))
            haveUp -= 1
    if haveDn >= zoneTiers
        float candDn = f_nearestBelow(close, gap, spaceDn, space)
        float farDn = usedDn.min()
        if not na(candDn) and candDn > farDn and close - farDn > atr * (capBaseATR + capStepATR * (haveDn - 1))
            for i = zones.size() - 1 to 0
                Zone z = zones.get(i)
                if not z.mitigated and z.isDemand and z.center == farDn
                    f_dropZone(i)
                    break
            usedDn.remove(usedDn.indexof(farDn))
            spaceDn.remove(spaceDn.indexof(farDn))
            haveDn -= 1
    if haveUp < zoneTiers
        for k = haveUp to zoneTiers - 1
            float cap  = atr * (capBaseATR + capStepATR * k)
            float cand = f_nearestAbove(close, gap, spaceUp, space)
            bool  proj = na(cand) or (cand - close) > cap
            float lvl  = proj ? close + cap : cand
            // Only a projected zone is pushed beyond existing tiers; a real level stays at its price.
            if proj and spaceUp.size() > 0
                lvl := math.max(lvl, spaceUp.max() + space)
            if not proj or lvl <= close + cap
                f_makeZone(lvl, false, proj)
                usedUp.push(lvl)
                spaceUp.push(lvl)
    if haveDn < zoneTiers
        for k = haveDn to zoneTiers - 1
            float cap  = atr * (capBaseATR + capStepATR * k)
            float cand = f_nearestBelow(close, gap, spaceDn, space)
            bool  proj = na(cand) or (close - cand) > cap
            float lvl  = proj ? close - cap : cand
            if proj and spaceDn.size() > 0
                lvl := math.min(lvl, spaceDn.min() - space)
            if not proj or lvl >= close - cap
                f_makeZone(lvl, true, proj)
                usedDn.push(lvl)
                spaceDn.push(lvl)

// Labels ride the right edge so they stay readable.
if zones.size() > 0
    for i = 0 to zones.size() - 1
        Zone z = zones.get(i)
        if not na(z.lb)
            label.set_x(z.lb, bar_index)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §5b KEY LEVELS  (hard prior-day / pivot lines — the reference's cyan levels)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Separate from the soft supply/demand bands: single, firm horizontal lines the
// market reacts to (prior-day high/low/close and, optionally, the floor pivots).
// Rebuilt once per session and extended right, so they sit as fixed reference rails.
var array<line>  klLines  = array.new<line>()
var array<label> klLabels = array.new<label>()

f_clearKeys() =>
    if klLines.size() > 0
        for i = 0 to klLines.size() - 1
            line.delete(klLines.get(i))
        klLines.clear()
    if klLabels.size() > 0
        for i = 0 to klLabels.size() - 1
            label.delete(klLabels.get(i))
        klLabels.clear()

f_keyLevel(_price, _txt, _clr, _style) =>
    if not na(_price)
        line ln = line.new(bar_index, _price, bar_index + 1, _price, color=_clr, width=1, style=_style, extend=extend.right, xloc=xloc.bar_index)
        klLines.push(ln)
        label lb = label.new(bar_index, _price, _txt, style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(_clr, 25), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small, xloc=xloc.bar_index)
        klLabels.push(lb)

// Rebuild the day's rails at each new session.
if showKeyLevels and isIntraday and isNewSession
    f_clearKeys()
    if klPDHL
        f_keyLevel(pdH, "PDH", klHLClr, line.style_solid)
        f_keyLevel(pdL, "PDL", klHLClr, line.style_solid)
    if klPDC
        f_keyLevel(pdC, "PDC", klHLClr, line.style_dotted)
    if klPivot
        f_keyLevel(pp, "PP", klPivClr, line.style_dashed)
        f_keyLevel(r1, "R1", klPivClr, line.style_dashed)
        f_keyLevel(s1, "S1", klPivClr, line.style_dashed)

// v2.2: opening-range rails, drawn once the range is complete (cleared with the day's other rails).
if showKeyLevels and isIntraday and klOR and inSession and dayLen == orBars and barstate.isconfirmed
    f_keyLevel(orHigh, "ORH", klORClr, line.style_dashed)
    f_keyLevel(orLow, "ORL", klORClr, line.style_dashed)

// Ride the key-level labels to the right edge so they stay readable.
if klLabels.size() > 0
    for i = 0 to klLabels.size() - 1
        label.set_x(klLabels.get(i), bar_index)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §6 LOCATION  (where price sits in the live map)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
float prox = atr * zoneProxATR
bool atDemand = false
bool atSupply = false
float tapDemandBot = na
float tapSupplyTop = na
float tapDemandC = na
float tapSupplyC = na
float nextUp = na
float nextDn = na
bool nextUpProjected = false
bool nextDnProjected = false
if zones.size() > 0
    for i = 0 to zones.size() - 1
        Zone z = zones.get(i)
        if not z.mitigated
            if close <= z.top + prox and close >= z.bot - prox
                if z.isDemand
                    atDemand := true
                    tapDemandBot := z.bot
                    tapDemandC := z.center
                else
                    atSupply := true
                    tapSupplyTop := z.top
                    tapSupplyC := z.center
            if not z.isDemand and z.bot > close and (na(nextUp) or z.bot < nextUp)
                nextUp := z.bot
                nextUpProjected := z.isProjected
            if z.isDemand and z.top < close and (na(nextDn) or z.top > nextDn)
                nextDn := z.top
                nextDnProjected := z.isProjected

locIdx = atDemand ? 0 : atSupply ? 2 : 1
locTxt = atDemand ? "AT DEMAND" : atSupply ? "AT SUPPLY" : "MID"
locClr = atDemand ? demandClr : atSupply ? supplyClr : neutralClr

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §6b INTRABAR PRESSURE
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Each sub-bar contributes signed effort weighted by its CLOSE POSITION, so a small
// candle with one-sided internals still registers while a large two-sided candle
// does not. When the feed returns too few sub-bars to judge (for example a 1-minute
// sub-bar request on a 1-minute chart) the reading is suppressed rather than
// reported from a degenerate one-bar sample.

ltfSigned = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, fpLtf, ((high - low) > 0 ? (2 * close - high - low) / (high - low) : 0.0) * (nz(volume) > 0 ? volume : (high - low)), ignore_invalid_timeframe=true)
ltfEffort = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, fpLtf, nz(volume) > 0 ? volume : (high - low), ignore_invalid_timeframe=true)

float fpNet = 0.0
float fpTot = 0.0
int   fpN   = 0
if not na(ltfEffort) and ltfEffort.size() > 0
    fpN := ltfEffort.size()
    for i = 0 to fpN - 1
        fpTot += nz(ltfEffort.get(i))
if not na(ltfSigned) and ltfSigned.size() > 0
    for i = 0 to ltfSigned.size() - 1
        fpNet += nz(ltfSigned.get(i))

fpValid = showFootprint and timeframe.in_seconds(fpLtf) < timeframe.in_seconds() and fpN >= fpMinSubBars and fpTot > 0
float fpAvg = ta.sma(fpTot, fpEffLen)
fpImbNow = fpTot > 0 ? fpNet / fpTot : 0.0
fpBig    = fpValid and (na(fpAvg) or fpTot >= fpAvg * fpEffMult)

pressBuy  = fpBig and fpImbNow >=  fpImbal and (not fpAtZoneOnly or atDemand)
pressSell = fpBig and fpImbNow <= -fpImbal and (not fpAtZoneOnly or atSupply)

// Sweep markers: price takes a zone edge then closes back through it.
fpUpWick = (high - math.max(open, close)) / rangeBar
fpDnWick = (math.min(open, close) - low) / rangeBar
sweepDemand = not na(tapDemandBot) and low  < tapDemandBot and close > tapDemandBot and fpDnWick >= 0.2
sweepSupply = not na(tapSupplyTop) and high > tapSupplyTop and close < tapSupplyTop and fpUpWick >= 0.2

// v2.2: confirmed sweeps. A sweep is only PENDING until a later bar (within sweepConfBars) closes
// beyond the sweep bar's high (demand) / low (supply). A close back through the zone, or running
// out of bars, cancels it. Each zone can confirm once per session.
f_farFromAll(array<float> _arr, float _v, float _tol) =>
    bool isFar = true
    if _arr.size() > 0
        for i = 0 to _arr.size() - 1
            if math.abs(_arr.get(i) - _v) <= _tol
                isFar := false
                break
    isFar

var float swDC   = na
var float swDBot = na
var float swDX   = na
var int   swDBar = na
var float swSC   = na
var float swSTop = na
var float swSX   = na
var int   swSBar = na
var array<float> swDoneD = array.new<float>()
var array<float> swDoneS = array.new<float>()
if isNewSession
    swDBar := na
    swSBar := na
    swDoneD.clear()
    swDoneS.clear()
bool sweepDemandConf = false
bool sweepSupplyConf = false
if not na(swDBar)
    if close < swDBot or bar_index - swDBar > sweepConfBars
        swDBar := na
    else if close > swDX
        sweepDemandConf := true
        swDoneD.push(swDC)
        swDBar := na
if not na(swSBar)
    if close > swSTop or bar_index - swSBar > sweepConfBars
        swSBar := na
    else if close < swSX
        sweepSupplyConf := true
        swDoneS.push(swSC)
        swSBar := na
if sweepDemand and na(swDBar) and not na(atr) and f_farFromAll(swDoneD, tapDemandC, atr * 0.7)
    swDC   := tapDemandC
    swDBot := tapDemandBot
    swDX   := high
    swDBar := bar_index
if sweepSupply and na(swSBar) and not na(atr) and f_farFromAll(swDoneS, tapSupplyC, atr * 0.7)
    swSC   := tapSupplyC
    swSTop := tapSupplyTop
    swSX   := low
    swSBar := bar_index
markSweepD = sweepConfOnly ? sweepDemandConf : sweepDemand
markSweepS = sweepConfOnly ? sweepSupplyConf : sweepSupply

plotshape(pressBuy and barstate.isconfirmed,  "Buy Pressure",  style=shape.circle, location=location.belowbar, color=demandClr, size=size.tiny)
plotshape(pressSell and barstate.isconfirmed, "Sell Pressure", style=shape.circle, location=location.abovebar, color=supplyClr, size=size.tiny)
plotshape(showFootprint and fpMarkTraps and markSweepD and barstate.isconfirmed, "Demand Sweep", style=shape.xcross, location=location.belowbar, color=demandClr, size=size.tiny)
plotshape(showFootprint and fpMarkTraps and markSweepS and barstate.isconfirmed, "Supply Sweep", style=shape.xcross, location=location.abovebar, color=supplyClr, size=size.tiny)

// v2: bar-close versions (final) + separate EARLY versions on the forming bar (may cancel).
alertcondition(pressBuy and barstate.isconfirmed,  "Buy Pressure (bar close)",  "Intrabar flow strongly one-sided up at a demand zone (bar closed).")
alertcondition(pressSell and barstate.isconfirmed, "Sell Pressure (bar close)", "Intrabar flow strongly one-sided down at a supply zone (bar closed).")
alertcondition(pressBuy and not barstate.isconfirmed,  "EARLY Buy Pressure (may cancel)",  "Forming bar shows one-sided buying at demand. Not final until the bar closes.")
alertcondition(pressSell and not barstate.isconfirmed, "EARLY Sell Pressure (may cancel)", "Forming bar shows one-sided selling at supply. Not final until the bar closes.")
alertcondition(showFootprint and fpMarkTraps and markSweepD and barstate.isconfirmed, "Demand Sweep (bar close)", "Demand zone swept and reclaimed (confirmed if 'Confirmed Sweeps Only' is on). Context, not a trade signal.")
alertcondition(showFootprint and fpMarkTraps and markSweepS and barstate.isconfirmed, "Supply Sweep (bar close)", "Supply zone swept and rejected (confirmed if 'Confirmed Sweeps Only' is on). Context, not a trade signal.")

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §6c PATH HISTORY  (descriptive, not a trading probability)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// One global episode prevents overlapping future windows across buckets too.
// Resolution alone never creates an observation. A transition while busy or without
// real barriers is skipped, not queued for when conditions become convenient.
stateId = regimeIdx * 9 + (flowState + 1) * 3 + locIdx

var array<int> hitUp = array.new<int>(27, 0)
var array<int> hitDn = array.new<int>(27, 0)
var array<int> timedOut = array.new<int>(27, 0)
var array<int> bothHit = array.new<int>(27, 0)
var array<int> sessionCut = array.new<int>(27, 0)
var array<int> sampleDays = array.new<int>(27, 0)
var array<int> lastSampleDay = array.new<int>(27, na)
var int prevState = na
var int pState = na
var float pUp = na
var float pDn = na
var int pBar = na

if useProb and barstate.isconfirmed
    // Never use tomorrow's opening gap to resolve yesterday's unfinished episode.
    if not na(pState) and (isNewSession or not inSession)
        sessionCut.set(pState, sessionCut.get(pState) + 1)
        pState := na
    if isNewSession or not inSession
        prevState := na
    if not na(pState)
        bool up = high >= pUp
        bool dn = low <= pDn
        bool done = true
        if up and dn
            bothHit.set(pState, bothHit.get(pState) + 1)
        else if up
            hitUp.set(pState, hitUp.get(pState) + 1)
        else if dn
            hitDn.set(pState, hitDn.get(pState) + 1)
        else if bar_index - pBar >= probHorizon
            timedOut.set(pState, timedOut.get(pState) + 1)
        else if sessionEnds
            sessionCut.set(pState, sessionCut.get(pState) + 1)
        else
            done := false
        if done
            pState := na
    bool changed = not na(prevState) and stateId != prevState
    bool realBarriers = not na(nextUp) and not na(nextDn) and nextDn < close and close < nextUp and not nextUpProjected and not nextDnProjected
    if inSession and not sessionEnds and changed and realBarriers and na(pState)
        pState := stateId
        pUp := nextUp
        pDn := nextDn
        pBar := bar_index
        int sampleDay = time("D")
        if na(lastSampleDay.get(stateId)) or lastSampleDay.get(stateId) != sampleDay
            sampleDays.set(stateId, sampleDays.get(stateId) + 1)
            lastSampleDay.set(stateId, sampleDay)
    if inSession
        prevState := stateId

// Keep the statistical bucket fixed during a forming bar.
statsState = barstate.isconfirmed ? stateId : nz(stateId[1], stateId)
nUp = hitUp.get(statsState)
nDn = hitDn.get(statsState)
nTimeout = timedOut.get(statsState)
nBoth = bothHit.get(statsState)
nCut = sessionCut.get(statsState)
nResolved = nUp + nDn
nFinished = nResolved + nTimeout + nBoth + nCut
nPending = not na(pState) and pState == statsState ? 1 : 0
resolvedShare = nResolved > 0 ? 100.0 * nUp / nResolved : na
// Bounds on the historical within-H up-first share: timeouts are known non-hits;
// both-hit bars and session cuts can be either up-first or not. Pending is separate.
historyLo = nFinished > 0 ? 100.0 * nUp / nFinished : na
historyHi = nFinished > 0 ? 100.0 * (nUp + nBoth + nCut) / nFinished : na
probReady = useProb and nFinished >= probMinN

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §7 PANEL
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
panelAnchor = switch panelPos
    "Top Left"      => position.top_left
    "Top Center"    => position.top_center
    "Top Right"     => position.top_right
    "Bottom Left"   => position.bottom_left
    "Bottom Center" => position.bottom_center
    => position.bottom_right

var table panel = table.new(panelAnchor, 2, 13, border_width=1)
f_row(_t, _r, _k, _v, _vclr) =>
    table.cell(_t, 0, _r, _k, text_color=color.white, text_size=size.small, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 20), text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(_t, 1, _r, _v, text_color=_vclr,       text_size=size.small, bgcolor=color.new(color.black, 20), text_halign=text.align_right)

if showPanel and barstate.islast
    f_row(panel, 0, "Regime", regimeTxt, regimeClr)
    f_row(panel, 1, useRealVol ? "Flow (volume proxy)" : "Flow (range proxy)", flowTxt, flowClr)
    f_row(panel, 2, "Location", locTxt, locClr)
    string upTxt = na(nextUp) ? "—" : str.tostring(math.round(nextUp - close, 1)) + (nextUpProjected ? " (proj)" : "")
    string dnTxt = na(nextDn) ? "—" : str.tostring(math.round(close - nextDn, 1)) + (nextDnProjected ? " (proj)" : "")
    f_row(panel, 3, "To Supply", upTxt, supplyClr)
    f_row(panel, 4, "To Demand", dnTxt, demandClr)
    string nTxt = useProb ? str.tostring(nFinished) + " done / " + str.tostring(nPending) + " open / " + str.tostring(sampleDays.get(statsState)) + " days" : "OFF"
    f_row(panel, 5, "History (closed state)", nTxt, neutralClr)
    string countTxt = useProb ? str.tostring(nUp) + " / " + str.tostring(nDn) + " / " + str.tostring(nTimeout) + " / " + str.tostring(nBoth) + " / " + str.tostring(nCut) : "—"
    f_row(panel, 6, "Up / Dn / Timeout / Both / Cut", countTxt, neutralClr)
    string pTxt = not useProb ? "OFF" : probReady and nResolved >= probMinN ? str.tostring(resolvedShare, "0") + "% (n=" + str.tostring(nResolved) + ")" : "Too few resolved episodes"
    f_row(panel, 7, "Up first | resolved only", pTxt, neutralClr)
    string boundsTxt = not useProb ? "OFF" : probReady ? str.tostring(historyLo, "0") + ".." + str.tostring(historyHi, "0") + "% (not a CI)" : "Too few finished episodes"
    f_row(panel, 8, "Up by H | history bounds", boundsTxt, neutralClr)
    f_row(panel, 9, "Forecast / edge / effective n", "Not established", neutralClr)
    f_row(panel, 10, "Divergence", bearDiv ? "BEARISH" : bullDiv ? "BULLISH" : "—", bearDiv ? supplyClr : bullDiv ? demandClr : neutralClr)
    string fpTxt = not fpValid ? "n/a (LTF unavailable/invalid)" : pressBuy ? (barstate.isconfirmed ? "BUY" : "BUY?") : pressSell ? (barstate.isconfirmed ? "SELL" : "SELL?") : "—"
    f_row(panel, 11, "Pressure | Gold", fpTxt + " | " + goldAnchorTxt, pressBuy ? demandClr : pressSell ? supplyClr : neutralClr)
    f_row(panel, 12, "Sampling", "Transitions; real zones; H=" + str.tostring(probHorizon), neutralClr)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// §8 ALERTS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Regime alerts fire on the hysteresis flip, not on every touch of the line.
// v2: all of these are evaluated on the bar close so they cannot fire and then un-happen.
goldFlipUp = regimeIdx == 2 and regimeIdx[1] != 2
goldFlipDn = regimeIdx == 0 and regimeIdx[1] != 0
alertcondition(goldFlipUp and barstate.isconfirmed, "Regime Turned Bullish", "Golden Line direction and slope agree bullish (bar closed).")
alertcondition(goldFlipDn and barstate.isconfirmed, "Regime Turned Bearish", "Golden Line direction and slope agree bearish (bar closed).")
alertcondition(bearDiv and barstate.isconfirmed, "Bearish Divergence", "Higher swing high on weaker cumulative delta (bar closed).")
alertcondition(bullDiv and barstate.isconfirmed, "Bullish Divergence", "Lower swing low on stronger cumulative delta (bar closed).")
